# forge/edge/flame: flame tongues (MYTHIC; 28.3): uneven tongues licking down, a tall one and a short one every 6 px,
# the hot core lit (step 4), closed in dark.
# FORGE-MARKS, forge i2 (tools: emb_P2c/forge/areas/FORGE-MARKS/tools2/mk2.py). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# EDGE STAMP (`overlay edge.<v>`, `on-edge:hem`): along the armour hang's lowest outline row (the torso's when no hang),
# column by column, the view's origin row on that row; cells may redraw two rows above it and add two below. Material
# cells (v w x y z: steps 0-4) draw in the hem's OWN slot (i1 drew Ink: black bars), K the ink, `-` notches (at or above
# the hem row), `.` keeps. Every added shape closes on a step-0 row or column of its own (the ring stays closed, C3a).
# The phase is the part's origin column, so the stamp is symmetric about the body.
# (FORGE-MARKS forge i3) tongues flicking right, period 4: a lit base, the tongue one column right, its dark tip.
use person
role overlay edge.flame
tags tile overlay edge on-edge:hem

























# (envelope r1, FORGE-MATERIAL; A5 "flame and sparkle pixels, 1 px speckle") the tongue re-cut as a plane: a 2 x 2 lit
# tongue on its flank under a 3 px lit lip, period 5, no step-4 point (the old z made a white speck every 4 px along every
# hem and its 1 px y tongue read as glitter); the fire's light is the view's own (render.cpp), not the hem's pixels.
# (FINISH wave-2 fix2 r2, C19 A5) the tongue a column wider on its flank and its tip lit inside the dark (vyv): a 3 x 2
# lit tongue closed in step 0, +2 lit px facing R on the Mythic's hem.
view D key rest origin 1 2
|.....
|.....
|yyyxw
|vyyyv
|.vyv.
